{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Computer Burble",
 "category": "Effects",
 "text": "Sound: the bubbling, stepping 'computer thinking' sound of sci-fi and acid: a resonant filter jumping to a new random place sixteen times a bar.\n\nHow it's built: a Sample & Hold takes a new random value (its own noise) on every Clock 1/16 and holds it; that staircase goes into the Ladder filter's CUTOFF, with RESONANCE high. The saw plays the key you hold.\n\nPlay: hold a low note.\n\nTweak: the clock's TEMPO and which output drives the Sample & Hold (1/8, 1/16); the filter's CV (how wide the jumps) and RESONANCE; put a Slew after the Sample & Hold to turn the steps into glides.",
